  "conclusions": [
    "The nineteen-photo intervention does not improve usable derived-mask output count: three for each learned arm versus six for production. No model integration.",
    "Mean observed material error changes only from 17.6341% to 17.6210%. Body IoU rises from 80.2687% to 80.6784%. Individual outcomes differ: boar material improves, green/pale star deteriorates.",
    "All thirteen checker predictions are identical because both held-out models train on the same six framed motifs. Corrected checker labels cannot improve their own held-out predictions.",
    "Sixteen of nineteen learned attempts fail before fitting. Ten candidate failures lack supported lobes/edges; six cannot identify both lower edges. Body and material fields, not solver search, are the immediate blockers.",
    "Accepted learned checker reconstructions visibly lose corner contact and erode cells into islands; a small error against that learned mask is misleading as a measure of source-design recovery.",
    "The new two-photo scenes and printed-paper correction have now been used in training the opposite-family model. They remain held out in their own inference model."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Previously inspected development photos, one seed, two broad source/motif folds; no unseen-test or physical-assembly claim.",
    "All pass counts are relative to a derived mask and the existing geometry/feature checks, not full ground-truth cutting paths.",
    "Changed grouping and corrected evaluation labels prevent direct comparison with the earlier 14.90% expanded-pilot error.",
    "Training-time label correction and two extra scenes form one intervention; this experiment does not isolate their individual effects.",
    "No production code, ONNX model, push or deployment."
  ],
  "nextExperiment": "Use the held-out body prediction only to propose a rough ROI; keep the unchanged photographic locator, classifier and geometric solver. Predeclare thresholds, padding and selection before inspecting results.",
